{"text": "Keawe did not believe the story at first, so he spoke to the bottle and said, I want my fifty dollars back. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> At once his pocket felt heavy again, and when he counted the money, he found exactly fifty dollars there. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Next he sold the bottle to a shop for sixty dollars, but it did come back, for that night it lay in his sea chest. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Keawe told everything to his friend Lopaka, a fellow sailor, who advised him to go home and wish for something good. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Back in Hawaii, Keawe heard sad news, for his uncle had died and his uncles son had drowned at sea. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Their land and money now belonged to Keawe, and it was exactly the amount that his dream house would cost. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Soon a grand house with three floors stood on the mountainside, and people called it the Bright House. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Lopaka wanted to buy the bottle, but first he asked to see the imp, and when it came out, both men froze with fear. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Even so, Lopaka bought it, because he dreamed of having a ship of his own, and he left that very night. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Keawe slept well for the first time in days, glad that the bottle was no longer his.", "alignment": {"characters": ["K", "e", "a", "w", "e", " ", "d", "i", "d", " ", "n", "o", "t", " ", "b", "e", "l", "i", "e", "v", "e", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "t", "o", "r", "y", " ", "a", "t", " ", "f", "i", "r", "s", "t", ",", " ", "s", "o", " ", "h", "e", " ", "s", "p", "o", "k", "e", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "b", "o", "t", "t", "l", "e", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "s", "a", "i", "d", ",", " ", "I", " ", "w", "a", "n", "t", " ", "m", "y", " ", "f", "i", "f", "t", "y", " ", "d", "o", "l", "l", "a", "r", "s", " ", "b", "a", "c", "k", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "A", "t", " ", "o", "n", "c", 